{
  "device_template": {
    "id": "fronius_solar_api_meter",
    "name": "Fronius Smart Meter (Solar API / HTTP-JSON)",
    "manufacturer": "Fronius",
    "description": "ONE HTTP request per poll to the Fronius DataManager's Solar API: GetMeterRealtimeData.cgi?Scope=Device&DeviceId=<id>. Built from a real capture (2026-10-22: DataManager card SW 3.34.1-5, Smart Meter TS 5kA-3, meter id 1). Use it when the meter cannot be read over Modbus; with Modbus available, fronius_sunspec_meter carries more (per-phase energies, average voltages).\n\nLOAD ON THE DATALOGGER: every register is in one poll group, so the meter costs exactly one GET per interval: 12 requests/min at the default 5 s, 30/min at 2 s. The inverters and the site poll the same web server, and the DataManager refreshes its values only about every 2.5 s, so polling faster than 5 s buys nothing. Keep it at 5 s or slower.\n\nTHE ID IN THE URL is the meter's Solar API id, as discovery reports it (1 on the captured installation, not 0). It is written into the URL literally; the unit stays the meter's Modbus address (240), so the device id and its history do not change when the meter moves between HTTP and Modbus. Do not put ${unit_id} in this source's URL: with unit 240 it would ask for DeviceId=240 and get nothing.\n\nSIGNS: power_active_total > 0 is import from the grid, < 0 is export. energy_active_import is the Consumed counter, energy_active_export the Produced one. Power factor is a ±1 fraction as the meter gives it, negative while importing.\n\nThe addresses are the SunSpec model-203 addresses of the same points (as in fronius_sunspec_meter), so a field keeps its identity (HA unique_id, InfluxDB series) whichever way the meter is read. Model and serial are text and cannot be read over this path. A GEN24 / Tauro datalogger names its meter fields differently (SMARTMETER_*) and needs its own template.\n\nNIGHT: the DataManager sleeps at night; the source goes offline like the other Solar API sources. No field is defaulted to zero.",
    "kind": "meter",
    "protocol": {
      "transports": [
        "http"
      ],
      "byte_order": "big"
    },
    "poll_groups": {
      "realtime": {
        "interval": 5,
        "description": "everything, in one request (the datalogger refreshes ~2.5 s; keep it at 5 s or slower)"
      }
    },
    "registers": [
